message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "TenderNet: data and code for 'Unconcentrated markets, captive buyers: incumbency in Türkiye's public IT procurement'"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-26
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aksoy
    given-names: Furkan
    email: furkan78177@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-0228-8202"
    affiliation: Maltepe University
  - family-names: Şimşek
    given-names: Arda
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-7969-6351"
    affiliation: Maltepe University
abstract: >-
  Code and derived data (9,991 EKAP IT contracts, 2010-2026). Supplier HHIs are low, but 45% of
  repeat-eligible contracts go to an incumbent versus 21% under a province-level permutation null;
  renewals (about one third) carry most of the excess, new needs still exceed their null, and prior
  supply multiplies a firm's odds of winning by about 24 in a conditional-logit choice model.
keywords:
  - public procurement
  - incumbency
  - vendor lock-in
  - market concentration
  - bipartite networks
  - Türkiye
  - EKAP
